      "problem": "\"Last time\" assumes this baker did the lesson before this one. The passage has no story group, and Papa Dorin isn't told what any baker has done before. He can give Isaiah 58:3 as context without saying the baker has already seen it.",
      "rule": {
        "link": "papa-dorin.md#what-he-knows",
        "text": "What he doesn't know: anything about the individual baker that he hasn't been told, such as their streak, their mood, the time of day or how they've done before. In lessons, he's never told, because every baker gets the same lesson."
      },
      "by": "opus",
      "at": {
        "stop": 1,
        "card": 1,
        "verses": "Isaiah 59:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "covered": true,
