        "card": 15
      },
      "problem": "The card cites only Isaiah 59:6, but \"Their feet are moving FAST\" comes from Isaiah 59:7 (\"Their feet run to evil; they are swift to shed innocent blood\"). The citation should be Isaiah 59:6-7.",
      "rule": {
        "link": "prep-walkthrough.md#scripture-rules",
        "text": "Cite exactly what the card uses. Every story card cites the verses it tells, from the first verse it uses to the last, no wider and no narrower."
      },
      "by": "opus",
      "at": {
        "stop": 1,
        "card": 15,
        "verses": "Isaiah 59:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "covered": true,
      "where": {
        "stop": 2,
        "card": 14
      },
      "problem": "The wrong answer \"At the city gate\" is close in meaning to \"In the public square.\" In Israel the city gate was the open public place where justice was done, so a baker could argue it's right. Use a wrong answer that's clearly a different kind of place.",
      "rule": {
        "link": "prep-walkthrough.md#answer-rules",
        "text": "No near-matches. A wrong answer never means the same as the right answer, or close to it. If a baker could argue it's right, replace it."
      },
      "by": "opus",
      "at": {
        "stop": 2,
        "card": 14,
        "verses": "Isaiah 59:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "covered": true,
      "where": {
        "stop": 3,
        "card": 4
      },
      "problem": "Card 3 says there was \"no man\" and \"no one to intercede,\" and the question repeats \"With no one to intercede.\" That rules out \"The king's arm\" and \"Isaiah's arm\" before the baker picks, which leaves only \"His own arm.\"",
      "rule": {
        "link": "prep-walkthrough.md#never-give-away-an-answer",
        "text": "A setup line can't rule out the wrong answers either."
      },
      "by": "opus",
      "at": {
