      "problem": "The first blank, \"righteousness,\" makes the baker guess the wording of the line. No earlier card tells that righteousness is part of the LORD's action. Card 3 left out \"His own righteousness sustained Him\" from Isaiah 59:16. Nothing in the setup points to righteousness over peace, glory or wisdom.",
      "rule": {
        "link": "prep-walkthrough.md#question-types",
        "text": "The rule against guessing the next words of a line (see below) applies to every passage, and to fill in the blank too. The blank tests meaning the baker can reason out, not wording they haven't seen."
